Jeremy renner's snow plow accident was  shocking to say the least and now the  star himself has given fans an update  about his condition Renner took to  Instagram on Tuesday January 3rd to  offer up his very first message to the  public since his serious snowplow  accident the star has been described as  being in critical but stable condition  following an accident involving the  snowplow on January 1st police officials  say Renner was near Mount Rose Highway  in Reno Nevada when the accident  occurred and that he suffered a serious  injury to his chest as Mr Renner always  does those private roads he was being a  great neighbor and he was plowing those  roads for his neighbor because up there  again they had three feet it was  subsequently reported that Renner  underwent surgery for blunt chest trauma  and Orthopedic injuries a representative  sent out a statement saying Jeremy's  family would like to express their  gratitude to the incredible doctors and  nurses looking after him they are also  tremendously overwhelmed and  appreciative of the outpouring of love  and support from his fans while while  things have appeared to be proceeding  smoothly with renner's treatment and the  start of his recovery many fans have  nonetheless been anxious to hear more  about how the star is doing thankfully  it now seems that the actor has  recovered enough to manage a reassuring  personal update on his own well-being as  well as the heartfelt thank you to  everyone via social media this has  prompted a deluge of support in the  comments on his Instagram page in the  new post the actor included a single  photo of himself in the hospital in  which he is severely bruised and hooked  up to medical equipment nevertheless  very much alive in a caption he wrote  thank you all for your kind words I'm  too messed up now to type but I send  love to you all an update from Renner  himself has proven to be a moment of  comfort for fans and what has otherwise  been an uneasy and concerning series of  updates regarding the actor's condition  the post garnered a startling amount of  attention amassing more than 5 million  seven hundred thousand likes and 230 000  comments within roughly 18 hours of  being posted while the actor remains in  critical condition it hopefully won't be  too long before fans get another update  about renner's recovery not long after  Renner broke his silence on the third  fans started flocking to his post to  show support one fan commented happy to  see you awake another said was really  worried about you even if we don't know  each other get well soon another fan  commented thinking of you every day man  sending love and prayers to my favorite  hero many fans were quick to invoke  renner's role as Hawkeye and the MCU in  their well wishes as one said get better  Hawkeye we all send our love and support  many of renner's colleagues from  throughout the film and entertainment  industry also took the time to comment  on the post fellow Marvel star Chris  Pratt said continued prayers your way  brother meanwhile Vanessa Hudgens wrote  sending so much love and healing and  actor Tasha Smith declared you're a  tough mother you know what and I love  you for it all in addition to showing  support many users and celebrities  expressed their happiness that Renner  was well in enough to provide his own  update celebrity trainer and actor Jason  Walsh posted damn brother I was really  worried about you good to see your face  and renner's tag co-star Isla Fisher  commented phew I'm so happy you made  this post sending you so much love and  healing energy we love you  [Music]
 

